## Exact bridge under investigation

```text
open isolate-involving upper equalities by an explicit finite contraction
  -> Audit.120's mandatory replacements must occur entirely inside the core
  -> a noncongruent full-source contact-isometry with no new core diameter
     pair contradicts the canonical diameter-pair minimum
  -> C-II closes if such an endpoint is supplied for every large canonical source
  -> Level I follows through the already closed C-I gate
```

This does not drop isolates: the contraction retains every isolate, checks every
isolate-involving lower pair, and moves no core point. Full-source extension of
the proposed core endpoint is still required.

The second deduction applies Audit.126 at the *actual new global minimizer*,
after isolate normalization. It does not transport arbitrary inactive pairs
back to the source without a displacement bound. A zero-width limit of that
audit gives an actual-diameter cubic moment and disperses a linear replacement
bank into a matching of order at least square root of D, regardless of move size.

